    "title": "<p>WHO Reporting System for Lung Cytopathology: Summary table of website feedback received on the beta version</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "IARC",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 775.8pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"1034\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.75pt; border: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">Chapter</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; border: solid gray 1.0pt; border-left: none; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">Heading</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 349.6pt; border: solid gray 1.0pt; border-left: none; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"466\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">Comment</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.75pt; border: solid gray 1.0pt; border-left: none; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">Date</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.95pt; border: solid gray 1.0pt; border-left: none; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"257\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">Response</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.75pt; border: solid gray 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">2.0.0.2: The role of lung cytopathology</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"116\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 349.6pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"466\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">Dear Sir / Madam If I may make a comment regarding one of the opening statements, cause I continuously see that the first world literature keeps on quoting it this way. This regards the statement of transthoracic FNAB: Transthoracic FNAB involves the introduction of a needle through the skin and chest wall into the pulmonary lesion under CT guidance, and is preferentially used for the diagnosis of peripheral nodules. TTNA (transthoracic) FNAB are performed either under CT guidance or under ultrasound guidance. Why is the ultrasound never mentioned? Our lung unit does a large number of transthoracic and transbronchial FNAB weekly and we have published extensively on this topic, but it's never mentioned. If the peripheral lung lesion abuts (and/or infiltrates the chest wall), there is no air between the probe and the lung mass and hence it can be seen with a ultrasound probe. The FNAB is then performed under ultrasound guidance. This is a much faster and cheaper procedure and our unit does vastly more ultrasound guided procedure(s) then CT guided procedures, which are more reserved for lesions that do not abut the chest wall. It would be more accurate to state that \"transthoracic FNAB can be performed either under CT-guidance or ultrasound guidance\" - that is if one wants to be more accurate and inclusive. Kind regards</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.75pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">2022-11-17 10:38:38</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.95pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"257\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">This is a helpful point, and we agree that transthoracic FNAB can use CT or ultrasound as FNAB does in other settings. However, CT is more commonly used for deeper lesions and we have made minor amendment to the text.</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.75pt; border: solid gray 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">8.1.1.2: Squamous cell carcinoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">Ancillary testing</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 349.6pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"466\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">Many labs do not have p40 stain Are there any criteria for p63 positivity like the p40 (50% positivity in tumor cells)?</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.75pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">2022-12-05 20:37:49</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.95pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"257\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">We have not found any information that might help. A study comparing the two in cytopathology specimens would be helpful.</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 76.75pt; border: solid gray 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"102\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">5.2.0.5: Salivary gland neoplasms</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 86.75pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"116\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">Key diagnostic cytopathological features</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 349.6pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"466\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">Beautiful photos, but should be omitted here and shifted to malignant chapter. Best regards</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 69.75pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"93\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">2022-12-21 09:45:37</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 192.95pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid gray 1.0pt; border-right: solid gray 1.0pt; padding: 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt 7.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"257\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;\">This was an error and the images concerned have been moved to the correct section.</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
